 "critic": "The strongest generated cues were interchangeable names, repeated full names, fixed rewards, and three-option menus that sometimes failed to address the same problem. Paying a theft victim or covering an unrelated shift felt like mechanically supplied alternatives. Several endings attached reputation or outsider status without making that relationship convincing. Exact duplicates and the repeated Friday-fee wording reinforced this impression. The fee requests still had clear economic causes and local pressure. Ivo's refusal, approaching deadline, threatened escalation, and neighbouring stalls resisting together made that card feel more specifically authored."
